Preheat oven to 350°; In a large bowl, combine chicken, soup, olives, green chilies, sour cream, half cup enchilada sauce; Mix thoroughly; Spread mixture evenly in each tortilla; Roll; Place in baking dish; Cover with remaining enchilada sauce; Spread Jack cheese evenly over enchiladas; Cover with foil and bake at 350° for 30 minutes or until cheese is melted;

Heat sauce in a skillet; Dip a tortilla in the sauce to make it easy to work with; Place tortilla on Dutch oven lid or plate, add meat, onion, cheese; Roll up and gently place in Dutch oven or pan; When pan is full, pour remaining sauce over enchiladas and sprinkle cheese; Heat until sauce bubbles or cheese melts;

