The directions of **Pork Roast with applesauce, molasses, ginger, garlic** are: Have meat market person loosen backbone of pork loin; Place roast, fat side up, on rack in open roasting pan in center of oven; Roast in 325° oven for 2 to 3 hours or until meat thermometer registers 170°; In saucepan, combine applesauce, molasses, ginger and garlic over medium heat; Brush pork every 10 minutes the last 30 minutes of cooking; Serve pork with remaining applesauce;

The directions of **Pork Roast (basic)** are: Trim fat from roast; Place in pan and pierce with a long fork;

The directions of **Pork Roast with brown sugar, salt, pepper, tomatoes, onion, Tabasco, catsup, water** are: Rub brown sugar into pork; Place in deep roasting pan. Sprinkle well with salt and pepper; Then add tomatoes, onion, Tabasco, catsup and water to the pan; Baste often with the mixture while baking; Roast in open roasting pan at 300° for 3 ½ hours or until well done

The directions of Gourmet Chili are: Heat oil in a 4 or 5-quart pot; Saute onion until clear, add peppers and garlic and saute until limp; Add chili powder, cumin, oregano, ground beef, salt and pepper; Cook slowly, stirring often, until meat is brown and broken apart; Add tomatoes and kidney beans, including liquid; Stir well to combine ingredients;

Saute onion and garlic until brown; Saute ground chuck until brown, then drain grease; Add all ingredients to meat; Simmer 45 minutes to 1 hour;

